<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link><description>World News Today: Read the latest world news headlines, Current International breaking news world wide. In depth analysis and top news headlines world wide.</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-08-21T22:51:22+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/296589292.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Fri, 21 Aug 2026 22:51:22 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[A mother who spent £170k on annexe for disabled daughter’s home in Worcester now faces demolition]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133408310.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A mother who spent £170,000 building a two-storey annexe for her disabled daughter could now be forced to demolish it after losing a planning appeal. Clair Birch, 59, built the one-bedroom annexe in the garden of her semi-detached home in Worcester. She said the building was designed to give her daughter more independence and meet her specific needs.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-mother-spent-170000-building-a-two-storey-annexe-to-give-her-disabled-daughter-a-safe-home-in-worcester-it-now-faces-demolition-after-neighbours-complain/articleshow/133408310.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-mother-spent-170000-building-a-two-storey-annexe-to-give-her-disabled-daughter-a-safe-home-in-worcester-it-now-faces-demolition-after-neighbours-complain/articleshow/133408310.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-21T21:28:03+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133408665,imgsize-166914.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 1890, US printed 120,000 unusual $100 'Watermelon' notes; only about 35 are known to survive]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133407330.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In October, a unique 1890 'Watermelon' $100 Treasury Note will be up for auction, presenting collectors with a rare opportunity. With only about thirty-five of these notes still in existence, this particular note symbolizes a significant political clash over monetary policy. Its distinct back design, reminiscent of watermelons, earned it this quirky nickname, making it a truly historic piece of currency.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1890-the-us-printed-120000-unusual-100-watermelon-notes-only-about-35-are-known-to-survive-and-one-is-returning-to-auction/articleshow/133407330.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1890-the-us-printed-120000-unusual-100-watermelon-notes-only-about-35-are-known-to-survive-and-one-is-returning-to-auction/articleshow/133407330.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-21T21:18:48+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133408508,imgsize-1631842.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Woman seen dumping garbage in a lake in Canada's Abbotsford fined for $1000, police sergeant says 'don't make it a race thing']]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133408285.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/woman-seen-dumping-garbage-in-a-lake-in-canadas-abbotsford-fined-for-1000-police-sergeant-says-dont-make-it-a-race-thing/articleshow/133408285.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/woman-seen-dumping-garbage-in-a-lake-in-canadas-abbotsford-fined-for-1000-police-sergeant-says-dont-make-it-a-race-thing/articleshow/133408285.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-21T21:08:28+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133408339,imgsize-41784.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Not just Indian techies, why the 'American Dream' died for Harry and Meghan Markle]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133407687.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The UK that awaits the Sussexes is hardly a triumphant restoration like the one that greeted Charles II post-Cromwell. The Sussexes will live privately and have to figure out how to pay their rent. The King won’t even give an allowance the way he does to the disgraced Prince Andrew, and their popularity is hitting rock bottom.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/random-musing-not-just-indian-techies-why-the-american-dream-died-for-harry-and-meghan-markle/articleshow/133407687.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/random-musing-not-just-indian-techies-why-the-american-dream-died-for-harry-and-meghan-markle/articleshow/133407687.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-21T20:38:12+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Nirmalya Dutta</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133407749,imgsize-158224.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Meet Caden Pohlkamp, the Texas seventh-grader who built an underwater robot to test...]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133407094.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In Texas, a resourceful seventh-grader has crafted an underwater robot to analyze pond water quality. This clever invention measures environmental variables at varying depths across twelve ponds. Results demonstrated that artificial fountains greatly enhance water quality and support aquatic life. This remarkable endeavor secured him a spot as a finalist for national junior innovator honors, with Caden Pohlkamp now seeking to expand his environmental robotics initiatives.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-caden-pohlkamp-the-texas-seventh-grader-who-built-an-underwater-robot-to-test-12-neighbourhood-ponds-fountains-were-linked-to-healthier-water/articleshow/133407094.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-caden-pohlkamp-the-texas-seventh-grader-who-built-an-underwater-robot-to-test-12-neighbourhood-ponds-fountains-were-linked-to-healthier-water/articleshow/133407094.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-21T20:08:12+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133407316,imgsize-374845.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Mirza Fakhrul Islam Alamgir sworn in as Bangladesh's 23rd President]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133407208.cms" 