-gabbard-as-ex-dni-shares-emotional-update-on-husbands-cancer-treatment/articleshow/133407009.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/who-saw-this-coming-laura-loomer-hounds-tulsi-gabbard-as-ex-dni-shares-emotional-update-on-husbands-cancer-treatment/articleshow/133407009.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-21T19:59:31+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133407117,imgsize-64788.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[The US offered a California family $4 million for its 6,300-acre island ranch; after they refused...]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133406806.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A federal jury awarded a California family $12.7 million for their Santa Cruz Island ranch.  The government had seized the 6,300-acre property using eminent domain in 1996.  This verdict concluded a decades-long property dispute between park officials and the Gherini family.  The family's ancestors had owned part of the island since the late 19th century.  The award allowed the National Park Service to gain full control of the land.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/the-us-offered-a-california-family-4-million-for-its-6300-acre-island-ranch-after-they-refused-the-government-seized-it-and-a-jury-awarded-them-12-7-million/articleshow/133406806.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/the-us-offered-a-california-family-4-million-for-its-6300-acre-island-ranch-after-they-refused-the-government-seized-it-and-a-jury-awarded-them-12-7-million/articleshow/133406806.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-21T19:49:59+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133406975,imgsize-1091665.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 1986, a family sold California's 53,000-acre Santa Rosa Island to the US for nearly $30 million]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133405130.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In 1986, the United States government acquired Santa Rosa Island for close to thirty million dollars. This pivotal purchase marked the end of longstanding private ranching and agricultural practices on the sprawling island. Following the removal of cattle in 1998 and the cessation of residency in 2011, efforts towards environmental restoration commenced. Today, the island stands as a protected national sanctuary and an important cultural landmark.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1986-a-ranching-family-sold-californias-53000-acre-santa-rosa-island-to-the-us-for-nearly-30-million-they-retained-about-7-acres-and-the-right-to-stay-for-another-25-years/articleshow/133405130.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1986-a-ranching-family-sold-californias-53000-acre-santa-rosa-island-to-the-us-for-nearly-30-million-they-retained-about-7-acres-and-the-right-to-stay-for-another-25-years/articleshow/133405130.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-21T19:32:24+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133406683,imgsize-930662.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Man claims Meta fired him after he refused to sign a Green Card letter for a Chinese visa worker, seeks $1 million in lawsuit]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133406370.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/man-claims-meta-fired-him-after-he-refused-to-sign-a-green-card-letter-for-a-chinese-visa-worker-seeks-1-million-in-lawsuit/articleshow/133406370.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/man-claims-meta-fired-him-after-he-refused-to-sign-a-green-card-letter-for-a-chinese-visa-worker-seeks-1-million-in-lawsuit/articleshow/133406370.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-21T19:20:56+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133406396,imgsize-190834.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Chicago's mayor carved six Xs into a runway; 12 years later, the airfield became a 40-acre park]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133405678.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Chicago's Meigs Field airport was controversially closed overnight in 2003.  Six X-shaped gouges rendered the runway unusable, stranding sixteen aircraft.  The city cited security concerns following the September 11 attacks for the closure.  Twelve years later, the former airfield became a natural landscape.  This site now features prairie, wetlands, and wildlife habitat for migratory birds.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2003-chicagos-mayor-sent-bulldozers-to-carve-six-giant-xs-into-an-airport-runway-overnight-stranding-16-planes-12-years-later-the-former-airfield-reopened-with-40-acres-of-prairie-wetlands-and-wildlife-habitat/articleshow/133405678.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2003-chicagos-mayor-sent-bulldozers-to-carve-six-giant-xs-into-an-airport-runway-overnight-stranding-16-planes-12-years-later-the-former-airfield-reopened-with-40-acres-of-prairie-wetlands-and-wildlife-habitat/articleshow/133405678.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-21T18:53:20+05:30</pubDate><